From c3c48b2449a0183d723e7bcff3a57a2011222284 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:12:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 105/107] fix(classifier): bound and escape refusal reasons,
 and skip stray graphs

Review round 3 of B204.

A refused model's load error listed every refused directory and echoed
labels_file verbatim (a manifest value up to about 1 MiB) into the
client's error body, and the "Not a model:" WARNING wrote manifest strings
unescaped, so a crafted labels_file could forge log lines. Now:

- echoed manifest values are cut to 120 bytes;
- control characters in paths and reasons are escaped (\xNN) in the load
  error, the require_layout message and the WARNING;
- the load error lists at most 5 directories, then "and N more", within
  2 KiB.

A directory holding a graph but no layout files at all (a stray or
partly downloaded graph) is not a manifest or labels failure, so it is no
longer warned about or listed as a refusal. The warning dedupe was
already keyed on (dir, reason), so a changed reason warns again.

test_classifier_layout checks the escaping, the cut, the 5-dir cap and
the stray graph on all three engines, and asserts the reason for a
manifest.json linked to a directory.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
